  <ferc:GeneralInformationOnPlantAndOperationsTextblock id="Tag15" contextRef="C1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt;"&gt;The Company owns an undersea natural gas gathering and transmission system, which includes the East Breaks Gathering System and three supply legs that connect to a 42&amp;#8208;inch diameter mainline. The Company gathers and&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt;"&gt;transports natural gas received from fields located in the Galveston, Garden Banks, High Island, West Cameron and East Breaks areas of the Gulf of America to a junction platform owned by the Company located in West Cameron&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 12pt;"&gt;Block 167. The Company provides gathering and transportation services as authorized by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC). The Company's major customers include natural gas marketers and producers.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:GeneralInformationOnPlantAndOperationsTextblock>
