&lt;td style="width: 7.04157%; height: 20px; text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;font style="width: 7.04157%; height: 20px; font-family: calibri; font-size: 14pt;"&gt;7.3%&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 5.92553%; height: 20px; text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: calibri; font-size: 14pt;"&gt;7.3%&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal" style="text-align: justify; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: calibri; font-size: 14pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Note 4 - Related Party Transactions&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal" style="text-align: justify; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: calibri; font-size: 14pt;"&gt;Balances in accounts receivable and accounts payable with Associated Companies include activities in the normal course of business. In addition, Genesis collects cash and makes disbursements on the Company's behalf as part of its operating activities or may make advances to the Company for purposes of the Company's capital investment. The Company also incurs certain overhead costs from an affiliate of Genesis. Net payables or advances are classified as current liabilities in the accompanying balance sheets given they are payable on demand. Historically, neither the Company nor Genesis has demanded repayment of these amounts. See Note 2, Cash Management, regarding settlement of associated company receivables and payables. At December 31, 2025 and 2024, the Company had accounts payable to associated companies of approximately $79.0 million and $59.1 million.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal" style="text-align: justify; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: calibri;"&gt;In 2025 and 2024, the Company recorded revenues from associated companies of $113,861 and $147,453.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal" style="text-align: justify; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: calibri; font-size: 14pt;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Note 5 - Regulatory Matters&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal" style="text-align: justify; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: calibri;"&gt;The Company is subject to the jurisdiction of the FERC in accordance with the Natural Gas Act of 1938 and the Natural Gas Policy Act of 1978. The Company operates certain natural gas pipelines under a FERC approved tariff.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal" style="text-align: justify; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: calibri;"&gt;On March 10, 2026, HIOS filed to conclude the Storm Damage Surcharge that was effective April 1, 2021, pursuant to the terms stipulated in its tariff.&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: calibri;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 18.6667px;"&gt;Under Section 18.5(d) of the GT&amp;amp;C, if the amount in the Storm Damage Surcharge account is less than $100,000 (either negative or positive), HIOS is permitted to reduce the Storm Damage Surcharge to $0.00/Dth and to refund or direct bill shippers the remaining balance. Such refunds or direct bills are required to be based pro rata on the actual quantities transported by HIOS for the applicable month.&amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: calibri;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 18.6667px;"&gt;The balance as of the end of February 2026 is $58,680 and the Company anticipates that the balance will be collected in the second quarter of 2026.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal" style="text-align: justify; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in;"&gt;&lt;strong style="font-family: calibri; font-size: 14pt;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Note 6 - Contingencies&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal" style="text-align: justify;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: calibri;"&gt;Certain conditions may exist as of the date the financial statements are issued, which may result in a loss to the Company but which will only be resolved when one or more future events occur or fail to occur. The Company's management and its legal counsel assess such contingent liabilities, and such assessment inherently involves an exercise of judgment. In assessing loss contingencies related to legal proceedings that are pending against the Company or un-asserted claims that may result in such proceedings, the Company's legal counsel evaluates the perceived merits of any legal proceedings or un-asserted claims as well as the perceived merits of the amount of relief sought or expected to be sought therein.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal" style="text-align: justify; tab-stops: .5in 1.0in 1.5in 2.0in 2.5in 3.0in 3.5in 4.0in 4.5in 5.0in 5.5in 6.0in 6.5in 7.0in;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: calibri;"&gt;If the assessment of a contingency indicates that it is probable that a material loss has been incurred and the amount of the liability can be estimated, then the estimated liability would be accrued and the nature of the contingent liability would be disclosed in the Company's financial statements.If the assessment indicates that a potentially material loss contingency is not probable, but is reasonably possible, or is probable but cannot be estimated, then the nature of the contingent liability, together with an estimate of the range of possible loss if determinable and material, would be disclosed.Loss contingencies considered remote are generally not disclosed or recorded unless they involve guarantees that are material to the Company, in which case the nature of the guarantee would be disclosed. The Company had no matters requiring loss contingency accruals at December 31, 2025.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: calibri;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Note 7 - Asset Retirement Obligations&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="Normal"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: calibri; font-size: 14pt;"&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;/u&gt;The change in the balance of the ARO liability, which is included in other non-current liabilities in the accompanying balance sheet is as follows:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 23.948%; height: 100px;" border="0"&gt;

&lt;tr style="height: 20px;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 23.1315%; height: 20px;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: calibri; font-size: 14pt;"&gt;(in thousands)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 5.50064%; height: 20px;"&gt;&lt;font style="text-decoration: underline; font-size: 14pt; font-family: calibri;"&gt;&lt;font style="width: 5.50064%; height: 20px;"&gt;&lt;font style="width: 5.50064%; height: 20px;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;font style="width: 5.50064%; height: 20px;"&gt;2025&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 4.13589%; height: 20px; text-align: left;"&gt;&lt;font style="text-decoration: underline; font-size: 14pt; font-family: calibri;"&gt;&lt;font style="width: 4.13589%; height: 20px;"&gt;&lt;font style="width: 4.13589%; height: 20px;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2024&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 20px;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 23.1315%; height: 20px;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: calibri; font-size: 14pt;"&gt;Balance, January 1&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 5.50064%; height: 20px; text-align: left;"&gt;&lt;font style="width: 5.50064%; height: 20px; font-family: calibri; font-size: 14pt;"&gt;$66,843&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 4.13589%; height: 20px; text-align: left;"&gt;&lt;font style="width: 4.13589%; height: 20px; font-family: calibri; font-size: 14pt;"&gt;$63,432&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
